WEBVTT

00:00:02.130 --> 00:00:07.060
The Bisidian are pirates who've repeatedly attacked and plundered Federation ships.

00:00:08.030 --> 00:00:10.320
In other words, enemies of the Federation!

00:00:13.850 --> 00:00:17.110
Enemy detection systems have picked up what appear to be Vagan mobile suits!

00:00:19.570 --> 00:00:21.250
Why did you save me?

00:00:21.870 --> 00:00:26.790
You're supposed be a dangerous enemy... but I feel a warmth from you.

00:00:35.070 --> 00:00:37.570
You know who that person was, don't you?

00:00:38.160 --> 00:00:42.540
The pilot of that mobile suit was Asemu Asuno.

00:00:42.540 --> 00:00:43.980
Your father. {check against last ep}{checked}

00:00:49.520 --> 00:00:51.360
The Mars settlement plan.

00:00:52.150 --> 00:00:56.280
The people left behind in the Mars Sphere in the wake of its failure

00:00:56.280 --> 00:00:58.820
formed the independent nation of Vagan,

00:00:58.820 --> 00:01:03.000
and launched a war against the Earth Federation government.

00:01:04.790 --> 00:01:07.250
70 years have already passed

00:01:07.250 --> 00:01:13.360
since the conflict began.

00:01:17.050 --> 00:01:20.930
todokasete kono mune ni

00:01:17.050 --> 00:01:20.930
Let your voice reach my heart

00:01:20.930 --> 00:01:24.430
kasuka ni nokoru kimi no koe wo

00:01:20.930 --> 00:01:24.430
though it lingers but faintly in the air

00:01:24.430 --> 00:01:27.850
yume ja nai genjitsu de

00:01:24.430 --> 00:01:27.850
In a world that I know is not a dream

00:01:27.850 --> 00:01:33.610
samayoitsuzuketeita

00:01:27.850 --> 00:01:33.610
I kept wandering

00:01:42.080 --> 00:01:45.370
tachidomaru no mo mae ni susumu koto mo

00:01:42.080 --> 00:01:45.370
Halting in your tracks and walking ahead proudly

00:01:45.370 --> 00:01:48.830
atozusari na ki ga shiteta

00:01:45.370 --> 00:01:48.830
both seemed too fearsome a choice

00:01:48.830 --> 00:01:52.300
tojikomerareta shikakui sora no shita

00:01:48.830 --> 00:01:52.300
Here on the board, where we are bound to

00:01:52.300 --> 00:01:55.550
iki wo hisometeta

00:01:52.300 --> 00:01:55.550
I tried to breathe softly to blend in

00:01:55.550 --> 00:02:02.970
tsumetai hoho wo tsutawaru kako no yowasa nugutte

00:01:55.550 --> 00:02:02.970
I swept away the weakness of the past trailing down my cheeks

00:02:02.970 --> 00:02:09.440
hikari sasu basho he kono te wo nobasu yo

00:02:02.970 --> 00:02:09.440
and held out my hands to the light

00:02:11.560 --> 00:02:15.030
todokasete kono mune ni

00:02:11.560 --> 00:02:15.030
Let your voice reach my heart

00:02:15.030 --> 00:02:18.530
kasuka ni nokoru kimi no koe wo

00:02:15.030 --> 00:02:18.530
though it lingers but faintly in the air

00:02:18.530 --> 00:02:21.950
yume ja nai genjitsu de

00:02:18.530 --> 00:02:21.950
In a world that I know is not a dream

00:02:21.950 --> 00:02:24.910
sagashitsuzuketeru

00:02:21.950 --> 00:02:24.910
I kept searching

00:02:25.540 --> 00:02:29.040
todokaseru sono mune ni

00:02:25.540 --> 00:02:29.040
I will let my feelings and my voice

00:02:29.040 --> 00:02:32.460
tashika na omoi boku no koe wo

00:02:29.040 --> 00:02:32.460
reach your heart

00:02:32.460 --> 00:02:35.880
owaranai genjitsu de

00:02:32.460 --> 00:02:35.880
Through days without end

00:02:35.880 --> 00:02:39.300
sakebitsuzuketeiku

00:02:35.880 --> 00:02:39.300
I will be proud, be strong

00:02:39.300 --> 00:02:45.140
ashita wo shinjite

00:02:39.300 --> 00:02:45.140
and have faith in the future

00:02:47.560 --> 00:02:52.950
Episode 35
 The Cursed
 Treasure

00:02:55.910 --> 00:02:58.610
My... father?

00:02:58.610 --> 00:03:02.330
Yes. But now he's stooped to becoming a pirate.

00:03:02.850 --> 00:03:04.530
I won't acknowledge him as part of the Asuno family. {I wont accept him/consider him as}

00:03:06.450 --> 00:03:08.330
Forget all about him.

00:03:08.330 --> 00:03:10.370
I won't let his name be spoken again.

00:03:11.090 --> 00:03:13.290
G-Grandpa!

00:03:13.890 --> 00:03:14.960
Mr. Flit!

00:03:14.960 --> 00:03:16.380
Be right there!

00:03:17.960 --> 00:03:19.020
What is it?

00:03:19.020 --> 00:03:20.300
Look at this!

00:03:20.720 --> 00:03:24.020
It must've stuck on during the fight with the pirate mobile suits.

00:03:24.020 --> 00:03:25.200
Is it dangerous?

00:03:25.200 --> 00:03:26.220
No, it's not.

00:03:26.220 --> 00:03:29.890
It could be a message capsule.

00:03:29.890 --> 00:03:31.390
I see.

00:03:31.390 --> 00:03:32.830
Hurry up and analyze it.

00:03:32.830 --> 00:03:33.820
Yes, sir.

00:03:33.820 --> 00:03:35.820
And one more thing...

00:03:35.820 --> 00:03:39.740
The AGE Builder is mo{u}lding new parts for the AGE-3.

00:03:40.100 --> 00:03:42.410
I think they'll be finished soon.

00:03:42.840 --> 00:03:45.880
Understood. Take care of that too.

00:03:45.880 --> 00:03:47.330
Grandpa!

00:03:47.330 --> 00:03:49.660
Why are you telling me to forget?

00:03:49.660 --> 00:03:51.750
He's my father, isn't he?

00:03:52.260 --> 00:03:55.230
You knew he was alive, so why?

00:04:03.590 --> 00:04:05.980
Your father died.

00:04:06.750 --> 00:04:09.930
As a brave soldier of the Federation Forces.

00:04:09.930 --> 00:04:11.760
What are you talking about?!

00:04:11.760 --> 00:04:13.270
I don't understand!

00:04:24.300 --> 00:04:27.290
No hostile objects in the surrounding area.

00:04:27.290 --> 00:04:29.490
Maintaining course for the Luna base.

00:04:29.490 --> 00:04:31.640
I sure was surprised.

00:04:31.640 --> 00:04:32.650
At what?

00:04:32.650 --> 00:04:35.020
Don't you find it interesting, Sergeant Major?

00:04:35.020 --> 00:04:36.500
You're eating <i>again</i> ?

00:04:36.500 --> 00:04:39.770
Former Commander Asuno's son, a pirate...

00:04:39.770 --> 00:04:40.650
I don't care.

00:04:40.650 --> 00:04:44.180
I don't stick my nose into other people's family problems.

00:04:44.180 --> 00:04:45.380
But you know...

00:04:45.830 --> 00:04:47.980
I still want to know more.

00:04:57.890 --> 00:05:01.070
Mr. Rody! About Kio's dad...

00:05:01.070 --> 00:05:05.840
Huh? Oh. He went missing in combat 13 years ago.

00:05:05.840 --> 00:05:07.490
He was considered killed in action.

00:05:07.490 --> 00:05:09.410
K-Killed?!

00:05:09.410 --> 00:05:12.290
Concentrate on your work, Wootbit!

00:05:12.290 --> 00:05:16.710
When a mechanic gets hurt, it's usually because his mind wandered on the job.

00:05:16.710 --> 00:05:17.610
Y-Yes, sir!

00:05:20.470 --> 00:05:23.940
<i>But it's real. Asemu is...</i>

00:05:31.330 --> 00:05:33.770
<i>My dad's alive...</i>

00:05:40.320 --> 00:05:43.860
<i>My mom would be happy too, if she knew.</i>

00:05:47.990 --> 00:05:50.070
<i>Forget all about him.</i>

00:05:50.480 --> 00:05:53.000
<i>Your father died.</i>

00:05:57.860 --> 00:05:58.870
Hey, Kio.

00:05:59.240 --> 00:06:02.400
Using the sphere without permission is against regulations.

00:06:02.400 --> 00:06:03.640
Aunt Unoa...

00:06:04.370 --> 00:06:07.300
You finally decided to tell your mom you're doing well?

00:06:08.650 --> 00:06:11.010
Judging by your face, I guess not. {I guess not, by looking at you}

00:06:11.710 --> 00:06:13.020
This is weird.

00:06:13.020 --> 00:06:15.980
Grandpa isn't happy that my dad's alive?{he cares more about killing vagan than his family. why else would he have raised you that way?}

00:06:16.600 --> 00:06:18.390
Why would he say that?

00:06:18.830 --> 00:06:22.790
I'm really happy to learn my brother's still alive.

00:06:22.790 --> 00:06:25.180
Dad probably feels the same way.

00:06:25.180 --> 00:06:26.820
Then why?

00:06:27.210 --> 00:06:31.060
When you grow up, things get complicated.

00:06:31.060 --> 00:06:33.740
Sometimes you can't express your feelings openly.

00:06:35.330 --> 00:06:36.720
I don't understand...

00:06:39.180 --> 00:06:40.250
Come on.

00:06:40.250 --> 00:06:42.400
I'll make you some cocoa in the sick bay.

00:06:43.570 --> 00:06:44.590
Come on, now.

00:06:46.620 --> 00:06:47.330
Okay.

00:06:55.610 --> 00:06:59.520
You said something pretty harsh to your grandson.

00:06:59.520 --> 00:07:02.430
Telling him to forget his own father...

00:07:03.920 --> 00:07:09.580
I'd like my wife, Emily, to hear about this.

00:07:09.580 --> 00:07:14.370
But whether she'd be happy to see her son like that...

00:07:14.370 --> 00:07:19.180
Any{ good} parent would be happy their child was alive, no matter what.

00:07:19.780 --> 00:07:23.290
Isn't it the same for his son Kio?

00:07:23.290 --> 00:07:26.250
This is my family's business.{TL Note: this means "I know you're right but I refuse to accept it."}

00:07:26.250 --> 00:07:27.710
Stay out of it.

00:07:28.520 --> 00:07:29.810
My apologies.

00:07:34.050 --> 00:07:35.640
What are you working on?

00:07:35.640 --> 00:07:39.480
An X-Transmitter developed by the technical section.

00:07:40.060 --> 00:07:45.040
Once it's installed, you'll be able to control multiple bits at once.{true parallelism}

00:07:45.700 --> 00:07:47.970
I'll test it out in the next operation.

00:07:47.970 --> 00:07:52.110
Master Zeheart. It's almost time for the briefing.

00:07:52.110 --> 00:07:53.570
I see.{why is that guy in a space suit?}

00:07:55.410 --> 00:07:58.490
<i>I didn't think we'd ever be working together.</i>

00:07:58.490 --> 00:08:03.420
That just shows how important Lord Ezelcant considers this operation.

00:08:03.420 --> 00:08:05.970
<i>That goes without saying.</i>

00:08:05.970 --> 00:08:09.630
<i>Listen. We'll make a pincer attack on the Diva.</i>

00:08:09.630 --> 00:08:14.500
<i>The plan is to attack from two directions at once, and draw out our prey.</i>

00:08:15.010 --> 00:08:16.920
<i>Your fleet will take the front side.</i>

00:08:16.920 --> 00:08:19.080
<i>My fleet will take the rear.{dohoho}</i>

00:08:19.080 --> 00:08:20.720
<i>Any objections so far?</i>

00:08:20.720 --> 00:08:21.430
None.

00:08:22.020 --> 00:08:27.400
<i>That old ship doesn't stand a chance against the strength of our two fleets.</i>

00:08:27.820 --> 00:08:32.030
Just remember that we're on the same side.

00:08:32.590 --> 00:08:35.380
<i>Provided that you don't hold us back.</i>

00:08:37.770 --> 00:08:41.120
Master Zeheart, after he talked to you like that, why didn't you—

00:08:41.120 --> 00:08:42.120
Leil!

00:08:42.120 --> 00:08:43.180
Fram!

00:08:44.600 --> 00:08:48.210
We've received new orders from Lord Ezelcant.

00:09:06.720 --> 00:09:09.760
I used to fight alongside Asemu.

00:09:10.890 --> 00:09:13.240
It's good that he's alive.

00:09:33.970 --> 00:09:34.920
Um...

00:09:34.920 --> 00:09:39.090
Why are you cleaning the ship, Mr. Obright? {YOU FOUND ME OUT. TEE HEE HEE and then he runs away}

00:09:39.090 --> 00:09:41.290
Normally, this stuff is automatically...

00:09:41.290 --> 00:09:43.350
Because this is my house.{;_;}{r.i.p remi}

00:09:44.010 --> 00:09:44.770
House?

00:09:44.770 --> 00:09:47.170
The crew here are my family.

00:09:47.170 --> 00:09:50.190
So they can come back at any time...

00:09:50.190 --> 00:09:54.360
I keep it clean, and wait for them to return.{( 　ﾟ,_ゝﾟ)}

00:09:55.300 --> 00:09:57.940
Family...? Return...?

00:09:58.710 --> 00:09:59.530
Kio!

00:09:59.530 --> 00:10:01.320
There you are.

00:10:01.320 --> 00:10:02.750
Wootbit!

00:10:02.750 --> 00:10:07.290
They told me to fetch you because 
the Gundam's new parts are ready.

00:10:10.690 --> 00:10:12.380
Thanks.

00:10:14.280 --> 00:10:15.190
Let's go.

00:10:15.190 --> 00:10:15.880
Yeah.

00:10:27.910 --> 00:10:28.970
You're late.

00:10:29.490 --> 00:10:31.400
You're the one who's going to be using this.{It's you who'll be using this.}

00:10:31.400 --> 00:10:33.070
Listen carefully to the explanation.

00:10:34.530 --> 00:10:36.490
Okay, are we ready?

00:10:37.190 --> 00:10:41.360
We call this newly molded equipment the G-{spot}Viper.{equipment = singular, card}

00:10:41.360 --> 00:10:45.410
It combines with the Core {Splendor}Fighter to form the AGE-3 Orbital.

00:10:45.410 --> 00:10:50.580
The Orbital is armed with a SigMaxiss long cannon and two beam sabers.{so like, does the AGE System come up with the names too?}

00:10:50.580 --> 00:10:55.000
Its main thrusters have high output, increasing its acceleration potential.

00:10:55.420 --> 00:10:58.440
And it has more thrusters everywhere, so it has better control.

00:10:59.020 --> 00:11:01.930
You'll be able to make tighter turns than you could before.

00:11:01.930 --> 00:11:08.370
Although it takes ground combat into account, it's mainly for fighting in space.

00:11:08.370 --> 00:11:11.510
So a high mobility type for space combat.

00:11:11.510 --> 00:11:12.880
That's right.

00:11:14.230 --> 00:11:18.030
Looks like the message capsule analysis finished too.

00:11:19.190 --> 00:11:20.450
Displaying video.

00:11:22.660 --> 00:11:23.880
Asemu...

00:11:25.840 --> 00:11:31.670
<i>If you're seeing this video, it means you've disabled the layers of protection I put on it.</i>

00:11:32.160 --> 00:11:33.580
<i>You pass.</i>

00:11:33.580 --> 00:11:36.110
<i>So I guess it's safe to tell you...{this makes no sense.}</i>

00:11:36.110 --> 00:11:39.170
<i>the secret intelligence we Bisidian have acquired.{you are good hackers, so I think I can trust you}</i>

00:11:39.170 --> 00:11:44.090
<i>The course of this war rests on a cursed treasure.</i>

00:11:47.540 --> 00:11:49.360
Cursed treasure...?

00:11:56.070 --> 00:11:58.360
A cursed treasure?

00:11:58.360 --> 00:12:03.410
Indeed. Depending on how it's used, it could lead all of space to ruin.

00:12:03.410 --> 00:12:07.700
But it also has the power to bring order to the world.

00:12:07.700 --> 00:12:10.960
So what is it, exactly?

00:12:10.960 --> 00:12:11.910
<i>It's called...</i>

00:12:11.910 --> 00:12:13.580
<i>the EXA-DB.</i>

00:12:13.960 --> 00:12:15.460
EXA-DB?

00:12:15.460 --> 00:12:21.800
<i>A huge database containing all the weapons data from before the Colony Nation Wars.{So like, euba/zalam shit?}{r.i.p don boyage}</i>

00:12:21.800 --> 00:12:26.470
Several hundred years ago, the Colony Nation Wars ended,

00:12:26.510 --> 00:12:31.480
and the Silver Chalice Treaty led to the abandonment of all weapons.

00:12:31.480 --> 00:12:37.900
But the documents and data that were to be destroyed along with the weapons

00:12:37.900 --> 00:12:41.530
were secretly compiled by the Federation government of the time,

00:12:41.530 --> 00:12:43.860
and left behind as the EXA-DB.

00:12:44.910 --> 00:12:52.500
<i>The EXA-DB is filled with mobile suit and warship blueprints, combat data, effective tactics...</i>

00:12:52.500 --> 00:12:56.210
<i>All the technology of the wars of the past.</i>

00:12:57.170 --> 00:13:03.300
<i>And eventually, it came to be known as the cursed treasure.</i>

00:13:03.590 --> 00:13:12.470
80 years ago, when Lord Ezelcant was investigating the corruption of the Federation Forces, he obtained part of it.

00:13:12.470 --> 00:13:18.650
That's how the Mars Sphere got its mobile suit and warship technology.

00:13:19.940 --> 00:13:26.070
So Vagan's military strength came 
from obtaining part of the EXA-DB?

00:13:26.070 --> 00:13:34.500
Vagan's engineers were able to develop new technology from part of that data.

00:13:34.960 --> 00:13:39.420
Then if somebody could obtain the entire EXA-DB...

00:13:39.420 --> 00:13:43.090
The power balance between the 
Federation and Vagan would change.

00:13:43.670 --> 00:13:49.010
If we could obtain it, it would contribute greatly to Lord Ezelcant's plan.

00:13:49.850 --> 00:13:52.180
So where is this EXA-DB now?

00:13:54.060 --> 00:13:55.020
<i>We don't know.</i>

00:13:56.310 --> 00:14:02.230
<i>All we know is that it's hidden on an asteroid floating somewhere in space.</i>

00:14:02.230 --> 00:14:06.780
<i>We found the asteroid once, but we lost it.</i>

00:14:06.780 --> 00:14:10.700
<i>The Federation and Vagan must be searching frantically for it right now.{Why haven't they been for the past 80 years?}{actually, they probably have been for over 80 years.}</i>

00:14:10.700 --> 00:14:14.620
<i>Given its contents, they won't make that public.</i>

00:14:15.000 --> 00:14:21.790
Special forces were doing it covertly, but now the search has been entrusted with our team.

00:14:22.170 --> 00:14:26.220
Those are the new orders from Lord Ezelcant, aren't they?

00:14:26.220 --> 00:14:27.720
Yes.

00:14:27.720 --> 00:14:33.140
Leil, I want you to form and lead a detachment to handle the search for the EXA-DB.

00:14:33.140 --> 00:14:34.260
Yes, sir!{hi}

00:14:34.260 --> 00:14:36.600
I won't let you down!

00:14:36.600 --> 00:14:37.730
Fram.

00:14:37.730 --> 00:14:38.480
Yes, sir.

00:14:38.850 --> 00:14:42.020
This is a vital secret, even among the Vagan.

00:14:42.020 --> 00:14:44.530
Revealing it, even to a comrade,

00:14:44.530 --> 00:14:46.900
would be considered leaking classified information.

00:14:47.280 --> 00:14:49.070
I'll keep that in mind.

00:14:49.070 --> 00:14:53.410
But our priority now is to complete the operation in front of us.

00:14:53.410 --> 00:14:54.490
Let's go.

00:14:54.490 --> 00:15:02.170
<i>Unless you want this war to end in a tragedy, you must secure or destroy the EXA-DB.</i>

00:15:02.750 --> 00:15:06.960
<i>With the AGE System in your hands, it may be possible.</i>

00:15:08.470 --> 00:15:09.840
That's the end of the video.

00:15:09.840 --> 00:15:12.930
The cursed treasure, EXA-DB...

00:15:12.930 --> 00:15:15.510
I had no idea anything like that existed.

00:15:15.510 --> 00:15:18.270
Whoever obtained it would control all of space.

00:15:18.270 --> 00:15:21.940
We must find the EXA-DB as soon as possible.{so... 1 episode and they'll find what vagan/the federation couldn't for like 80 years?}{maybe 2 episodes}

00:15:21.940 --> 00:15:23.900
The EXA-DB...

00:15:24.440 --> 00:15:26.440
I wonder where it is...{This is not a question, wootbit}

00:15:28.490 --> 00:15:29.740
What's going on?

00:15:29.740 --> 00:15:31.200
Signals on enemy detection systems!

00:15:31.200 --> 00:15:33.910
One warship and 15 mobile suits behind us!

00:15:33.910 --> 00:15:36.080
High probability they're Vagan!

00:15:42.670 --> 00:15:45.340
Now come on out, Gundam!

00:15:47.250 --> 00:15:49.170
Maximum combat speed! Shake them off!

00:15:49.170 --> 00:15:51.930
Wait! Signals ahead as well!

00:15:51.930 --> 00:15:53.840
High probability they're Vagan, too!

00:15:53.840 --> 00:15:55.970
A pincer attack?!

00:15:55.970 --> 00:15:58.680
Captain, prepare to fire the photon blaster!

00:15:58.680 --> 00:15:59.270
Hurry!

00:16:00.430 --> 00:16:04.100
It's the only way to escape being surrounded!{front/back... how about up down left and right? this isn't LoGH}

00:16:05.480 --> 00:16:07.520
He's going ahead of schedule...

00:16:07.520 --> 00:16:10.150
Zanald's in too much of a hurry for glory.

00:16:11.610 --> 00:16:14.280
Very well, then. We'll strike them head on!

00:16:14.280 --> 00:16:16.620
Zeheart Galette, Ghirarga, heading out!

00:16:21.000 --> 00:16:23.460
Seric Abis, Clanche Custom, heading out!

00:16:28.300 --> 00:16:30.130
<i>Listen, Kio.</i>

00:16:30.130 --> 00:16:32.090
<i>Your top priority is defending the ship.</i>

00:16:32.090 --> 00:16:36.220
<i>Just buy time until the photon blaster is ready to fire.</i>

00:16:36.220 --> 00:16:38.810
<i>Don't get too far away from the Diva!</i>

00:16:38.810 --> 00:16:39.970
Right!

00:16:39.970 --> 00:16:41.310
Kio Asuno. Here I go!

00:17:25.100 --> 00:17:27.650
Enemy mobile suits are in firing range!

00:17:27.650 --> 00:17:29.650
Open all gunports!

00:17:29.650 --> 00:17:30.570
Open fire, please!

00:17:43.500 --> 00:17:45.080
There are still so many!

00:17:45.080 --> 00:17:47.040
Calm down. You're doing fine.

00:17:47.040 --> 00:17:49.630
Don't forget to maintain a barrage.

00:17:49.630 --> 00:17:50.000
Right!

00:17:51.380 --> 00:17:54.050
Jonathan and I will hit the enemy behind us.

00:17:54.510 --> 00:17:58.800
Mr. Obright and Derek, help Kio protect the ship from the enemy ahead!

00:17:58.800 --> 00:17:59.640
Roger!

00:18:04.560 --> 00:18:05.310
He's coming!{XDDD}

00:18:05.310 --> 00:18:06.060
I can feel it!

00:18:06.480 --> 00:18:07.850
It's him.

00:18:07.850 --> 00:18:09.440
Zeheart Galette!{why does he remember his full name?}

00:18:10.650 --> 00:18:14.030
I'm glad you came to our side, Gundam!

00:18:27.080 --> 00:18:29.580
The Gundam went to the other side?

00:18:29.580 --> 00:18:32.000
I won't let Zeheart get him!

00:18:34.250 --> 00:18:36.210
Is that a mobile suit?

00:18:36.380 --> 00:18:38.090
I-It's huge!

00:18:38.090 --> 00:18:40.510
Out of the way, small fry!

00:18:44.350 --> 00:18:45.680
Jonathan!

00:18:45.680 --> 00:18:46.980
<i>I can still fight!</i>

00:18:49.940 --> 00:18:51.230
Bastard!

00:19:02.820 --> 00:19:06.120
Let's try out the X-Transmitter!

00:19:13.790 --> 00:19:14.960
What?

00:19:28.730 --> 00:19:31.100
It's faster than the last type I saw.

00:19:31.100 --> 00:19:32.350
A high mobility type?

00:19:34.360 --> 00:19:36.020
The enemy's an X-Rounder!

00:19:36.020 --> 00:19:39.690
But the Ghirarga's fast, too! {ghiraga wontw lose in speed!}{"won't lose in speed" sounds dumb}

00:19:41.490 --> 00:19:42.410
No, you don't!

00:19:50.580 --> 00:19:51.830
He fell for it.{what a dumbass. inb4 big ass guy from other side comes barreling down and screws up THE HEART}

00:19:51.830 --> 00:19:53.210
Fire the wires!{FIREWIRE XD}

00:20:05.140 --> 00:20:06.300
What?!{lolderp}

00:20:41.090 --> 00:20:42.050
Not bad.

00:20:42.050 --> 00:20:44.930
You've improved even more since last time!

00:20:48.810 --> 00:20:50.600
<i>Kio! You're too far away from the Diva!</i>

00:20:50.600 --> 00:20:51.310
<i>Get back!</i>

00:21:04.200 --> 00:21:07.120
I won't let you get away, Gundam!

00:21:12.540 --> 00:21:14.330
Former Commander Asuno, where are you going?

00:21:14.330 --> 00:21:16.750
The enemy's trying to capture the Gundam!

00:21:16.750 --> 00:21:17.880
I'm heading out, too!

00:21:20.710 --> 00:21:22.710
Did you hear that, Mr. Obright?

00:21:22.710 --> 00:21:23.470
Derek?

00:21:23.470 --> 00:21:25.130
Bring Kio back now!

00:21:28.010 --> 00:21:29.970
I've got my hands full here!

00:21:30.970 --> 00:21:33.140
Shit—there's too many!

00:21:45.200 --> 00:21:46.570
At this rate, I won't make it!

00:21:46.950 --> 00:21:48.910
I have to pick one, defeat it...

00:21:49.410 --> 00:21:50.830
and create an opening!

00:21:52.740 --> 00:21:55.500
You thought I'd be easier to defeat?

00:21:55.500 --> 00:21:56.410
However!

00:22:00.670 --> 00:22:04.460
There are more ways to attack than just beams and swords!

